No — `withClient` in db.js:11-16 never releases the client if `fn(client)` throws, since there's no try/finally. That's why idle stays at 0 and waiting climbs steadily in pool.log; it's a leak, not a capacity problem. Raising `max` would just delay the same failure.

Fix:

```js
async function withClient(fn) {
  const client = await pool.connect();
  try {
    return await fn(client);
  } finally {
    client.release();
  }
}
```

